      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A direct W/CuCrZr interface is prone to high interfacial stresses.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A direct W/CuCrZr interface is prone to unwanted interdiffusion.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A refractory HEA is suitable for use under the elevated-temperature and irradiation conditions associated with fusion reactors.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10142552::chunk::001::introduction::6f0510eec9",
        "PMC10154406::chunk::000::abstract::f895614108"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "A refractory HEA interlayer can be compositionally graded to transition properties between W and CuCrZr.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Laser powder bed fusion can fabricate the proposed graded refractory-HEA interlayer.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fusion-reactor service exposes the joint to high heat flux, elevated temperature, and irradiation.",
